      "player": "Gem25P Drama",
      "type": "llm_response",
      "reasoning": "I passed priority to my opponent, a silent challenge. And they, in their folly, have taken the bait. They have cast a spell, `Pick Your Poison`. They have paid the mana. Now, as the spell sits on the stack, the game turns its eye to me. It asks me if I wish to respond.\n\
\n\
The answer is a resounding, deafening, \"no\".\n\
\n\
Why would I counter this? Let them choose. Let them destroy an artifact, an enchantment, or... a creature with flying. They see my `Restless Anchorage`, tapped from its assault. They see the map token, a trinket. They believe they have me. They believe they have a choice.\n\
\n\
They are wrong. They have no good choices. The `Anchorage` is not a creature right now. It is a land. The map token is a pittance. Whatever they choose, it is a minor inconvenience, a fly to be swatted away. I will not waste my precious resources on this. I will let their spell resolve. I will let them have this small, hollow victory. It will make their inevitable defeat all the more crushing.\n\
\n\
I pass. The weight of this \"no\" is the weight of a spider, motionless in its web, watching a fly struggle. The fly thinks it can escape. The spider knows better. I pass. Now. Let's see what they choose. It matters not. The outcome is already decided.",
