    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Discarding Elspeth, Storm Slayer is a significant mistake. Elspeth is a powerful 5-mana planeswalker that creates tokens (doubled by her static ability), buffs creatures, and removes threats. Against what appears to be a control mirror or slow matchup, Elspeth represents a must-answer threat that can win the game on her own. The player has 4 lands with Sunken Citadel potentially providing extra mana, meaning Elspeth could be cast soon. The player already has redundant copies of cards like No More Lies (2 copies) and Fountainport (2 copies), making those much better discard candidates. Discarding a duplicate Fountainport loses almost nothing since you already have one and have limited land drops remaining, whereas Elspeth is a unique, high-impact card.",
      "action_taken": "Discarded Elspeth, Storm Slayer",
      "better_line": "Discard a duplicate Fountainport or the second No More Lies. Fountainport is a land that enters untapped but the player already has two copies and likely won't need both. Keeping Elspeth as a win condition is far more valuable than a redundant land or counterspell.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 57,
      "player": "Gem25P Drama",
      "decision_index": 56,
    },
