      "description": "In a control mirror at a board stall, Gem3F Valley declined to activate Restless Reef (4/4 deathtouch) and attack. With 10 lands available, activating Reef for 4 mana would leave 6 mana open — enough for Three Steps Ahead to counter any removal the opponent might have. The opponent is at 14 life, so each 4-damage attack is significant pressure. Missing a free attack in a control mirror where win conditions are scarce is a meaningful tempo loss.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority during combat without activating Restless Reef or attacking.",
      "better_line": "Activate Restless Reef for {2}{U}{B}, attack with it (dealing 4 damage and milling 4), while holding up Three Steps Ahead or other countermagic with remaining 6 mana to protect it from removal.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 195,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 213,
    },
    {
      "severity": "moderate",
      "description": "Gem3F Valley passed the turn in postcombat main with 10 lands available and multiple useful actions. They could have played Watery Grave from hand (land drop), activated Restless Reef as a 4/4 deathtouch attacker (though combat is over, this wouldn't help offensively), or most importantly cast Wan Shi Tong, Librarian at end of opponent's turn for value. However, the critical miss is not playing the Watery Grave land from hand - it's a free land drop that increases future mana availability. Additionally, they could activate Fountainport to create a Fish token or Treasure token as a mana sink, or activate Demolition Field to destroy one of the opponent's nonbasic lands (Restless Anchorage, Sunken Citadel, Fountainport, etc.) which would slow down the opponent's creature-land beatdown plan while also triggering Wan Shi Tong if cast later. Passing with an unplayed land drop and available mana sinks wastes resources.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in postcombat main, ending the turn without taking any action.",
      "better_line": "Play Watery Grave from hand (paying 2 life or tapped), then use remaining mana to activate Demolition Field targeting one of opponent's Restless Anchorages or other key nonbasic lands, or at minimum use Fountainport as a mana sink to create a token/treasure. Could also hold up Wan Shi Tong + counter magic by playing the land first to have more mana available next turn.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 197,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 215,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem25P Drama passed priority in precombat main with 15 lands on the battlefield and mana available, missing the opportunity to cast Consult the Star Charts (potentially kicked) at end of opponent's turn or at least activate Fountainport to create a token/treasure, or use Demolition Field to destroy one of the opponent's nonbasic lands (like Restless Reef or Fountainport). While some of these could be done at instant speed later, using Demolition Field is a particularly strong play here since the opponent has key utility lands like Fountainport and Restless Reef, and Gem25P Drama has a Demolition Field available to use proactively.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority without taking any action in precombat main phase.",
      "better_line": "Activate Demolition Field targeting opponent's Restless Reef or Fountainport to deny them a key utility/creature land, or at minimum plan to use mana on Consult the Star Charts (kicked) at end of opponent's next turn. Could also animate Restless Anchorage to attack and generate Map tokens.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 198,
      "player": "Gem25P Drama",
      "decision_index": 216,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "In a control mirror with an empty board, Gem3F Valley passed combat without activating Restless Reef to attack. Restless Reef as a 4/4 deathtouch is an excellent attacker - if unblocked it deals 4 damage and mills 4, and if blocked by Restless Anchorage (2/3), deathtouch kills the Anchorage while Reef survives. With 10 lands available, they could activate Reef (4 mana) and still hold up 6 mana for Three Steps Ahead or Essence Scatter.",
      "action_taken": "Passed combat without attacking, wasting an opportunity for free pressure.",
      "better_line": "Activate Restless Reef for {2}{U}{B} and attack. Either deal 4 damage + mill 4, or trade favorably with an opponent's creature land. Keep 6 mana up for countermagic.",
