    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "In a control mirror at turn 23, casting a flash creature (Wan Shi Tong) during their own postcombat main phase taps them out completely, leaving no mana to protect it or interact on the opponent's turn. The opponent has plenty of mana and potential answers. While the ETB card draw provides value regardless, Wan Shi Tong has flash and could be cast at the end of the opponent's next turn instead, allowing Valley to untap and have countermagic mana available to protect it.",
