      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 212,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 227,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Wan Shi Tong, Librarian is on the stack (cast for a large X, resulting in the opponent drawing 7 cards and getting a massive flying vigilance creature). Gem3F Valley has Essence Scatter in hand and plenty of untapped mana to cast it, but appears to not counter this game-defining threat.",
      "action_taken": "Tapped Gloomlake Verge for U without using Essence Scatter to counter Wan Shi Tong, allowing it to resolve and draw 7 cards",
      "better_line": "Cast Essence Scatter to counter Wan Shi Tong, Librarian, preventing the opponent from getting a huge flying creature and drawing 7 cards",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 231,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Wan Shi Tong, Librarian is on the stack and Gem3F Valley has Essence Scatter in hand with mana available to cast it. Wan Shi Tong is a massive threat - it's a flyer with vigilance that draws cards and grows whenever the opponent searches their library (which Gem3F Valley's Demolition Fields would trigger). In a control mirror where both players have been grinding for many turns with empty boards, letting a large creature resolve when you have a counter in hand is a critical error. The game note says 'Gem3F Valley draws seven cards' after this, suggesting Wan Shi Tong was cast for X=14 or similar huge value, making it an enormous flying threat that also drew many cards on entry.",
      "action_taken": "Declined to counter Wan Shi Tong, Librarian despite having Essence Scatter and Three Steps Ahead available.",
      "better_line": "Cast Essence Scatter targeting Wan Shi Tong, Librarian to counter this major threat. Alternatively, cast Three Steps Ahead in counter mode to counter it.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 213,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 231,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem25P Drama's opponent just cast Wan Shi Tong, Librarian (on the stack), and Drama has Three Steps Ahead and No More Lies in hand with mana available to counter it. Wan Shi Tong is a significant threat that draws cards and grows whenever the opponent searches their library (Drama has multiple Demolition Fields that trigger searches). Instead of countering this must-answer threat, Drama passed priority, allowing it to resolve. Additionally, Drama has Day of Judgment, Elspeth, and other sorcery-speed plays available but is passing in postcombat main.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority while opponent's Wan Shi Tong, Librarian was on the stack, allowing it to resolve uncountered.",
      "better_line": "Counter Wan Shi Tong with Three Steps Ahead (counter mode for {1}{U}{U}) or No More Lies ({W}{U}) to prevent the opponent from establishing a card-drawing threat that also punishes Drama's Demolition Field activations.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 215,
      "player": "Gem25P Drama",
      "decision_index": 222,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Gem3F Valley has 2 untapped lands (Undercity Sewers and Island) and 3 copies of Three Steps Ahead in hand, each castable for {U} with the draw-two mode costing +{2} (total {3}{U}). With only 2 mana available, they can't use the draw mode. However, they have an unplayed land in hand (Island, Gloomlake Verge, or Restless Reef) that they should play before passing. They're holding 10 cards and will need to discard down to 7 at end of turn anyway. Playing a land drop costs nothing and increases future mana availability. Additionally, with Wan Shi Tong on board as a threat, having more mana untapped on the opponent's turn is valuable for protecting it with countermagic.",
      "action_taken": "Passed priority in postcombat main phase without playing a land, despite having Island, Gloomlake Verge, and Restless Reef in hand.",
      "better_line": "Play Restless Reef (or another land) from hand before passing. This provides additional mana on future turns and a creature-land threat, and reduces the number of cards that must be discarded to hand size.",
      "type": "blunder",
      "snapshot_index": 215,
      "player": "Gem3F Valley",
      "decision_index": 233,
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Discarded Restless Reef (a creature-land that serves as an additional win condition) instead of a basic land like Island or Gloomlake Verge. With 13 lands already in play, the mana from any additional land is marginal, but Restless Reef's ability to become a 4/4 deathtouch creature provides significant strategic value as a backup threat that dodges board wipes.",
