      "decision_index": 237,
    },
    {
      "severity": "major",
      "description": "Gem25P Drama passed the turn in postcombat main with Day of Judgment in hand and enough mana to cast it, while the opponent has a Wan Shi Tong, Librarian on the battlefield. Wan Shi Tong is a significant threat that draws cards and grows whenever the opponent searches their library (e.g., from Demolition Field activations). The opponent has multiple Demolition Fields. Leaving Wan Shi Tong alive lets it accumulate value. Day of Judgment costs {2}{W}{W} and Drama has access to Hallowed Fountain x3, Plains, Sunken Citadel (which can produce white), and Island - more than enough untapped mana to cast it. Additionally, Drama could have cast Consult the Star Charts or activated other abilities. Passing here wastes the opportunity to remove the only creature on the board.",
